    ],
    "industrial_process_notes": "The 'direct process' for synthesizing organosilicon/siloxane compounds was developed in the 1940s (associated with Eugene Rochow at General Electric and Richard Muller in Germany), founding the modern silicone industry. Commercial PDMS synthesis typically uses ring-opening polymerization of cyclic siloxanes catalyzed by alkali metal oxides.",
    "synthesis_scheme_image": null
  },
